IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc4-s84-definitions`

-- ccc4-s109-110-3-prohibition-orders.l4 -- sections 109 to 110.3 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (PART III, Firearms and Other Weapons):
-- Prohibition Orders: the mandatory order (109), the discretionary order (110), the emergency prohibition order (110.1), and the orders protecting information about it (110.2, 110.3).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone.  Sections 110.4 to 117.15 are another part's.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
--
-- Conventions: as in ccc4-s85-98-use-possession.l4.  Section 109(1) and 110(1) are duties of the court, so they are encoded twice: as a decision function over the facts
-- (what the court must do, answered MAYBE BOOLEAN) and as a regulative rule (PARTY `the court` MUST ...), which is run with #TRACE in the tests.
-- Judgments the text hands to the court ("desirable", "satisfied", "considers") are plain inputs.  The class and the maximum punishment of the offence, and the
-- answers of sections 2 and 3.01, are inputs named for the section they come from.

§ `Section 109 -- Mandatory prohibition order`

-- Whether an offence is "an indictable offence": the Code does not say how an offence that is both indictable and punishable on summary conviction counts (the words "hybrid"
-- and "dual procedure" occur nowhere in the text).  Reading A, taken: such an offence is an indictable offence when the proceeding is by indictment (fork F-hybrid).
-- src:2285 | Prohibition Orders
-- src:2286 | Mandatory prohibition order
-- src:2287 | 109 (1) Where a person is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of
-- src:2288 | (a) an indictable offence in the commission of which violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted and for which the person may be sentenced to imprisonment for ten years or more,
@ref s 109(1)(a) and (a.1), "an indictable offence" (src:2285-2288)
GIVEN `the class of the offence, by the section that creates it` IS A `Class of offence`
      `the mode of proceeding` IS A `Mode of proceeding`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109(1) the offence is an indictable offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the class of the offence, by the section that creates it`
    WHEN `an indictable offence` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an offence punishable on summary conviction` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an indictable offence in the commission of which violence against a person was used" (an offence punishable only on summary conviction is not indictable)
    WHEN `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction` THEN
        IF `the mode of proceeding` EQUALS `by indictment`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the text does not say how an offence that is both indictable and punishable on summary conviction counts when it is prosecuted summarily

-- (a) ... for which the person may be sentenced to imprisonment for ten years or more
-- src:2285 | Prohibition Orders
-- src:2286 | Mandatory prohibition order
-- src:2287 | 109 (1) Where a person is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of
-- src:2288 | (a) an indictable offence in the commission of which violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted and for which the person may be sentenced to imprisonment for ten years or more,
@ref s 109(1)(a), "imprisonment for ten years or more" (src:2285-2288)
GIVEN `the maximum imprisonment the person may be sentenced to for the offence` IS AN Imprisonment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109(1)(a) the maximum imprisonment is ten years or more` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the maximum imprisonment the person may be sentenced to for the offence`
    WHEN `imprisonment for life` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `no imprisonment is stated` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the offence states no imprisonment
    WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` term THEN
        BRANCH
            IF term's years TIMES 12 PLUS term's months GREATER THAN 120 THEN JUST TRUE
            IF term's years TIMES 12 PLUS term's months EQUALS 120 AND (term's days GREATER THAN 0 OR (NOT term's `less a day`)) THEN JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for which the person may be sentenced to imprisonment for ten years or more" (a term below ten years, or ten years less a day)

-- the person is convicted, or discharged under section 730
-- src:2285 | Prohibition Orders
-- src:2286 | Mandatory prohibition order
-- src:2287 | 109 (1) Where a person is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of
@ref s 109(1), "convicted, or discharged under section 730" (src:2285-2287)
DECLARE `s 109(1) how the person comes before the court for sentence` IS ONE OF
    `s 109(1) the person is convicted`
    `s 109(1) the person is discharged under section 730`
    `s 109(1) the person is neither convicted nor discharged under section 730`

-- (a) an indictable offence in the commission of which violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted and for which the person may be sentenced to imprisonment for ten years or more
-- src:2285 | Prohibition Orders
-- src:2286 | Mandatory prohibition order
-- src:2287 | 109 (1) Where a person is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of
-- src:2288 | (a) an indictable offence in the commission of which violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted and for which the person may be sentenced to imprisonment for ten years or more,
@ref s 109(1)(a) (src:2285-2288)
GIVEN `s 109(1) the offence is an indictable offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 3.01(1) the offence counts as an offence in the commission of which violence is used, threatened or attempted against any person or class of persons` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 109(1)(a) the maximum imprisonment is ten years or more` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109(1)(a) the offence is one in which violence was used and for which the person may be sentenced to imprisonment for ten years or more` MEANS
    `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST `s 109(1) the offence is an indictable offence`, (`s 84(1) some limb holds` (LIST (JUST `violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted in the commission of the offence`), `s 3.01(1) the offence counts as an offence in the commission of which violence is used, threatened or attempted against any person or class of persons`)), `s 109(1)(a) the maximum imprisonment is ten years or more`)   -- propagates: the answers of the sections the limb reads

-- (a.1) an indictable offence in the commission of which violence was used, threatened or attempted against (i) the person’s intimate partner, (ii) a child or parent of the person or of anyone referred to in subparagraph (i), or (iii) any person who resides with the person or with anyone referred to in subparagraph (i) or (ii)
-- src:2285 | Prohibition Orders
-- src:2286 | Mandatory prohibition order
-- src:2287 | 109 (1) Where a person is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of
@ref s 109(1)(a.1) (src:2285-2287)
-- src:2289 | (a.1) an indictable offence in the commission of which violence was used, threatened or attempted against
-- src:2290 | (i) the person’s intimate partner,
-- src:2291 | (ii) a child or parent of the person or of anyone referred to in subparagraph (i), or
-- src:2292 | (iii) any person who resides with the person or with anyone referred to in subparagraph (i) or (ii),
@ref s 109(1)(a.1) (src:2289-2292)
GIVEN `s 109(1) the offence is an indictable offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 3.01(1) the offence counts as an offence in the commission of which violence is used, threatened or attempted against any person or class of persons` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 intimate partner: the person against whom the violence was used, threatened or attempted is the person’s intimate partner` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person against whom the violence was used, threatened or attempted is a child or parent of the person or of the person’s intimate partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person against whom the violence was used, threatened or attempted resides with the person or with the person’s intimate partner, child or parent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109(1)(a.1) the offence is one in which violence was used against an intimate partner, a child or parent, or a person who resides with them` MEANS
    `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST `s 109(1) the offence is an indictable offence`, (`s 84(1) some limb holds` (LIST (JUST `violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted in the commission of the offence`), `s 3.01(1) the offence counts as an offence in the commission of which violence is used, threatened or attempted against any person or class of persons`)), (`s 84(1) some limb holds` (LIST `s 2 intimate partner: the person against whom the violence was used, threatened or attempted is the person’s intimate partner`, (JUST `the person against whom the violence was used, threatened or attempted is a child or parent of the person or of the person’s intimate partner`), (JUST `the person against whom the violence was used, threatened or attempted resides with the person or with the person’s intimate partner, child or parent`))))   -- propagates: the answers of the sections the limb reads

-- (b) an offence under subsection 85(1), 85(2), 95(1), 99(1), 100(1), 102(1), 102.1(1), 102.1(2), 103(1) or 104.1(1) or section 264 (criminal harassment)
-- src:2285 | Prohibition Orders
-- src:2286 | Mandatory prohibition order
-- src:2287 | 109 (1) Where a person is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of
@ref s 109(1)(b) (src:2285-2287)
-- src:2293 | (b) an offence under subsection 85(1) (using firearm in commission of offence), 85(2) (using imitation firearm in commission of offence), 95(1) (possession of prohibited or restricted firearm with ammunition), 99(1) (weapons trafficking), 100(1) (possession for purpose of weapons trafficking), 102(1) (making automatic firearm), 102.1(1) (possession of computer data), 102.1(2) (distribution of computer data), 103(1) (importing or exporting knowing it is unauthorized) or 104.1(1) (altering cartridge magazine) or section 264 (criminal harassment),
@ref s 109(1)(b) (src:2293)
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109(1)(b) the offence is one of those the paragraph names` MEANS
    IF     (`the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 85 AND (`the offence`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)" OR `the offence`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2)"))
        OR (`the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 95 AND `the offence`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
        OR (`the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 99 AND `the offence`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
        OR (`the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 100 AND `the offence`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
        OR (`the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 102 AND `the offence`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
        OR (`the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 102.1 AND (`the offence`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)" OR `the offence`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2)"))
        OR (`the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 103 AND `the offence`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
        OR (`the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 104.1 AND `the offence`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
        OR `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 264
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an offence under subsection 85(1) ... 85(2) ... 95(1) ... 99(1) ... 100(1) ... 102(1) ... 102.1(1) ... 102.1(2) ... 103(1) ... or 104.1(1) ... or section 264" (the list of offences of paragraph (b), the paragraph names no others)

-- Paragraphs (c) and (c.1) name offences under two other Acts, which are not among the sources: an offence is named by the Act, the section and the subsection.
-- src:2285 | Prohibition Orders
-- src:2286 | Mandatory prohibition order
-- src:2287 | 109 (1) Where a person is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of
@ref s 109(1)(c) and (c.1), the other Acts (src:2285-2287)
-- src:2294 | (c) an offence relating to the contravention of subsection 5(1) or (2), 6(1) or (2) or 7(1) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act,
-- src:2295 | (c.1) an offence relating to the contravention of subsection 9(1) or (2), 10(1) or (2), 11(1) or (2), 12(1), (4), (5), (6) or (7), 13(1) or 14(1) of the Cannabis Act, or
@ref s 109(1)(c) and (c.1), the other Acts (src:2294-2295)
DECLARE `s 109(1) another Act` IS ONE OF
    `s 109(1) the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act`
    `s 109(1) the Cannabis Act`
    `s 109(1) another Act of Parliament`

DECLARE `s 109(1) a contravention of another Act` HAS
    `the Act`          IS A `s 109(1) another Act`
    `the section`      IS A NUMBER
    `the subsection`   IS A STRING

-- (c) an offence relating to the contravention of subsection 5(1) or (2), 6(1) or (2) or 7(1) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act
@ref s 109(1)(c) (src:2294)
GIVEN contravention IS A `s 109(1) a contravention of another Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109(1)(c) the offence relates to the contravention of a subsection of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act that the paragraph names` MEANS
    IF     contravention's `the Act` EQUALS `s 109(1) the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act`
       AND (   (contravention's `the section` EQUALS 5 AND (contravention's `the subsection` EQUALS "(1)" OR contravention's `the subsection` EQUALS "(2)"))
            OR (contravention's `the section` EQUALS 6 AND (contravention's `the subsection` EQUALS "(1)" OR contravention's `the subsection` EQUALS "(2)"))
            OR (contravention's `the section` EQUALS 7 AND contravention's `the subsection` EQUALS "(1)"))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsection 5(1) or (2), 6(1) or (2) or 7(1) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act" (the paragraph names no other subsection)

-- (c.1) an offence relating to the contravention of subsection 9(1) or (2), 10(1) or (2), 11(1) or (2), 12(1), (4), (5), (6) or (7), 13(1) or 14(1) of the Cannabis Act
@ref s 109(1)(c.1) (src:2295)
GIVEN contravention IS A `s 109(1) a contravention of another Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109(1)(c.1) the offence relates to the contravention of a subsection of the Cannabis Act that the paragraph names` MEANS
    IF     contravention's `the Act` EQUALS `s 109(1) the Cannabis Act`
       AND (   (contravention's `the section` EQUALS 9 AND (contravention's `the subsection` EQUALS "(1)" OR contravention's `the subsection` EQUALS "(2)"))
            OR (contravention's `the section` EQUALS 10 AND (contravention's `the subsection` EQUALS "(1)" OR contravention's `the subsection` EQUALS "(2)"))
            OR (contravention's `the section` EQUALS 11 AND (contravention's `the subsection` EQUALS "(1)" OR contravention's `the subsection` EQUALS "(2)"))
            OR (contravention's `the section` EQUALS 12 AND (contravention's `the subsection` EQUALS "(1)" OR contravention's `the subsection` EQUALS "(4)" OR contravention's `the subsection` EQUALS "(5)" OR contravention's `the subsection` EQUALS "(6)" OR contravention's `the subsection` EQUALS "(7)"))
            OR (contravention's `the section` EQUALS 13 AND contravention's `the subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
            OR (contravention's `the section` EQUALS 14 AND contravention's `the subsection` EQUALS "(1)"))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsection 9(1) or (2), 10(1) or (2), 11(1) or (2), 12(1), (4), (5), (6) or (7), 13(1) or 14(1) of the Cannabis Act" (the paragraph names no other subsection)

-- (d) an offence that involves, or the subject-matter of which is, a firearm, a cross-bow, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition, any prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance and, at the time of the offence, the person was prohibited by any order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament from possessing any such thing
-- src:2285 | Prohibition Orders
-- src:2286 | Mandatory prohibition order
-- src:2287 | 109 (1) Where a person is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of
@ref s 109(1)(d) (src:2285-2287)
-- src:2296 | (d) an offence that involves, or the subject-matter of which is, a firearm, a cross-bow, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition, any prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance and, at the time of the offence, the person was prohibited by any order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament from possessing any such thing,
-- src:2297 | the court that sentences the person or directs that the person be discharged, as the case may be, shall, in addition to any other punishment that may be imposed for that offence or any other condition prescribed in the order of discharge, make an order prohibiting the person from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition and explosive substance during the period specified in the order as determined in accordance with subsection (2) or (3), as the case may be.
@ref s 109(1)(d) (src:2296-2297)
GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
      `the offence involves, or its subject-matter is, that thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time of the offence the person was prohibited by an order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament from possessing any such thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109(1)(d) the offence involves a thing the person was prohibited from possessing` MEANS
    IF     (`the thing is one that the paragraph names`)
       AND `the offence involves, or its subject-matter is, that thing`
       AND `at the time of the offence the person was prohibited by an order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament from possessing any such thing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an offence that involves, or the subject-matter of which is, a firearm" (the paragraph is met only by an offence of that kind, committed while prohibited)
    WHERE
        -- a firearm, a cross-bow, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition, any prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance
        `the thing is one that the paragraph names` MEANS
               `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a firearm` `the kind of thing`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a cross-bow`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited weapon`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a restricted weapon`
               OR `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a prohibited device` `the kind of thing`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a firearm part`
               OR `s 84(1) the kind of thing is ammunition or prohibited ammunition` `the kind of thing`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: an explosive substance`

-- Paragraphs (a) to (c.1) taken together: subsection 110(1) refers to them ("other than an offence referred to in any of paragraphs 109(1)(a) to (c.1)").
