-- src:2289 | (a.1) an indictable offence in the commission of which violence was used, threatened or attempted against
-- src:2290 | (i) the person’s intimate partner,
-- src:2291 | (ii) a child or parent of the person or of anyone referred to in subparagraph (i), or
-- src:2292 | (iii) any person who resides with the person or with anyone referred to in subparagraph (i) or (ii),
-- src:2293 | (b) an offence under subsection 85(1) (using firearm in commission of offence), 85(2) (using imitation firearm in commission of offence), 95(1) (possession of prohibited or restricted firearm with ammunition), 99(1) (weapons trafficking), 100(1) (possession for purpose of weapons trafficking), 102(1) (making automatic firearm), 102.1(1) (possession of computer data), 102.1(2) (distribution of computer data), 103(1) (importing or exporting knowing it is unauthorized) or 104.1(1) (altering cartridge magazine) or section 264 (criminal harassment),
-- src:2294 | (c) an offence relating to the contravention of subsection 5(1) or (2), 6(1) or (2) or 7(1) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act,
-- src:2295 | (c.1) an offence relating to the contravention of subsection 9(1) or (2), 10(1) or (2), 11(1) or (2), 12(1), (4), (5), (6) or (7), 13(1) or 14(1) of the Cannabis Act, or
@ref s 109(1)(a) to (c.1) (src:2285-2295)
GIVEN `s 109(1)(a) the offence is one in which violence was used and for which the person may be sentenced to imprisonment for ten years or more` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 109(1)(a.1) the offence is one in which violence was used against an intimate partner, a child or parent, or a person who resides with them` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 109(1)(b) the offence is one of those the paragraph names` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 109(1)(c) the offence relates to the contravention of a subsection of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act that the paragraph names` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 109(1)(c.1) the offence relates to the contravention of a subsection of the Cannabis Act that the paragraph names` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109(1) the offence is referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (c.1)` MEANS
    `s 84(1) some limb holds` (LIST `s 109(1)(a) the offence is one in which violence was used and for which the person may be sentenced to imprisonment for ten years or more`, `s 109(1)(a.1) the offence is one in which violence was used against an intimate partner, a child or parent, or a person who resides with them`, `s 109(1)(b) the offence is one of those the paragraph names`, `s 109(1)(c) the offence relates to the contravention of a subsection of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act that the paragraph names`, `s 109(1)(c.1) the offence relates to the contravention of a subsection of the Cannabis Act that the paragraph names`)   -- propagates: the answers of paragraphs (a) to (c.1)

-- Where a person is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of an offence within (a) to (d), the court that sentences the person or directs that the person be discharged shall make a prohibition order.
-- src:2285 | Prohibition Orders
-- src:2286 | Mandatory prohibition order
-- src:2287 | 109 (1) Where a person is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of
-- src:2288 | (a) an indictable offence in the commission of which violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted and for which the person may be sentenced to imprisonment for ten years or more,
-- src:2289 | (a.1) an indictable offence in the commission of which violence was used, threatened or attempted against
-- src:2290 | (i) the person’s intimate partner,
-- src:2291 | (ii) a child or parent of the person or of anyone referred to in subparagraph (i), or
-- src:2292 | (iii) any person who resides with the person or with anyone referred to in subparagraph (i) or (ii),
-- src:2293 | (b) an offence under subsection 85(1) (using firearm in commission of offence), 85(2) (using imitation firearm in commission of offence), 95(1) (possession of prohibited or restricted firearm with ammunition), 99(1) (weapons trafficking), 100(1) (possession for purpose of weapons trafficking), 102(1) (making automatic firearm), 102.1(1) (possession of computer data), 102.1(2) (distribution of computer data), 103(1) (importing or exporting knowing it is unauthorized) or 104.1(1) (altering cartridge magazine) or section 264 (criminal harassment),
-- src:2294 | (c) an offence relating to the contravention of subsection 5(1) or (2), 6(1) or (2) or 7(1) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act,
-- src:2295 | (c.1) an offence relating to the contravention of subsection 9(1) or (2), 10(1) or (2), 11(1) or (2), 12(1), (4), (5), (6) or (7), 13(1) or 14(1) of the Cannabis Act, or
-- src:2296 | (d) an offence that involves, or the subject-matter of which is, a firearm, a cross-bow, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition, any prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance and, at the time of the offence, the person was prohibited by any order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament from possessing any such thing,
-- src:2297 | the court that sentences the person or directs that the person be discharged, as the case may be, shall, in addition to any other punishment that may be imposed for that offence or any other condition prescribed in the order of discharge, make an order prohibiting the person from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition and explosive substance during the period specified in the order as determined in accordance with subsection (2) or (3), as the case may be.
@ref s 109(1) (src:2285-2297)
GIVEN `how the person comes before the court for sentence` IS A `s 109(1) how the person comes before the court for sentence`
      `s 109(1) the offence is referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (c.1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 109(1)(d) the offence involves a thing the person was prohibited from possessing` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109(1) the court must make a prohibition order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `how the person comes before the court for sentence` EQUALS `s 109(1) the person is neither convicted nor discharged under section 730` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of" (a "where" that fails)
        IF `the offence is within (a) to (d)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the offence is within (a) to (d)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the answer of a paragraph or of a section it reads is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of" an offence within paragraphs (a) to (d) (an offence outside them: the mandatory order is not required by this subsection)
    WHERE
        `the offence is within (a) to (d)` MEANS `s 84(1) some limb holds` (LIST `s 109(1) the offence is referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (c.1)`, `s 109(1)(d) the offence involves a thing the person was prohibited from possessing`)

-- The duty of the court as a regulative rule.  The text fixes no time for it ("in addition to any other punishment"), so there is no WITHIN.
DECLARE `s 109 act of the court or of a justice` IS ONE OF
    `s 109 make an order prohibiting the person from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition and explosive substance`
    `s 110 consider whether it is desirable to make an order prohibiting the person from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance`
    `s 110 make the order that the court decides is desirable`
    `s 110 include in the record a statement of the court’s reasons for not making the order or not prohibiting everything`
    `s 110.1 make an emergency prohibition order`
    `s 110.1 make a report to a justice`
    `s 110.2 place the documents in a packet and seal it`
    `s 110.3 place the originals in a packet and seal it`

-- src:2285 | Prohibition Orders
-- src:2286 | Mandatory prohibition order
-- src:2287 | 109 (1) Where a person is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of
-- src:2288 | (a) an indictable offence in the commission of which violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted and for which the person may be sentenced to imprisonment for ten years or more,
-- src:2289 | (a.1) an indictable offence in the commission of which violence was used, threatened or attempted against
-- src:2290 | (i) the person’s intimate partner,
-- src:2291 | (ii) a child or parent of the person or of anyone referred to in subparagraph (i), or
-- src:2292 | (iii) any person who resides with the person or with anyone referred to in subparagraph (i) or (ii),
-- src:2293 | (b) an offence under subsection 85(1) (using firearm in commission of offence), 85(2) (using imitation firearm in commission of offence), 95(1) (possession of prohibited or restricted firearm with ammunition), 99(1) (weapons trafficking), 100(1) (possession for purpose of weapons trafficking), 102(1) (making automatic firearm), 102.1(1) (possession of computer data), 102.1(2) (distribution of computer data), 103(1) (importing or exporting knowing it is unauthorized) or 104.1(1) (altering cartridge magazine) or section 264 (criminal harassment),
-- src:2294 | (c) an offence relating to the contravention of subsection 5(1) or (2), 6(1) or (2) or 7(1) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act,
-- src:2295 | (c.1) an offence relating to the contravention of subsection 9(1) or (2), 10(1) or (2), 11(1) or (2), 12(1), (4), (5), (6) or (7), 13(1) or 14(1) of the Cannabis Act, or
-- src:2296 | (d) an offence that involves, or the subject-matter of which is, a firearm, a cross-bow, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition, any prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance and, at the time of the offence, the person was prohibited by any order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament from possessing any such thing,
-- src:2297 | the court that sentences the person or directs that the person be discharged, as the case may be, shall, in addition to any other punishment that may be imposed for that offence or any other condition prescribed in the order of discharge, make an order prohibiting the person from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition and explosive substance during the period specified in the order as determined in accordance with subsection (2) or (3), as the case may be.
@ref s 109(1), the duty (src:2285-2297)
GIVEN `subsection (1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 109 act of the court or of a justice`
`s 109(1) the duty of the court to make a prohibition order` MEANS
    IF `subsection (1) applies`
    THEN PARTY `the court`
         MUST `s 109 make an order prohibiting the person from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition and explosive substance`
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `Section 109(2) to (4) -- Duration of the prohibition order`

-- How long the order prohibits possession of a thing.
DECLARE `s 109 period of the prohibition` IS ONE OF
    `s 109 period: for life`
    `s 109 period: ending not earlier than` HAS `the earliest day on which the period may end` IS A DATE

-- (2) In the case of a first conviction for or discharge from the offence: (a) any firearm other than a prohibited firearm or restricted firearm, and any crossbow, restricted weapon, firearm part, ammunition and explosive substance, during the period that
-- (i) begins on the day on which the order is made, and (ii) ends not earlier than ten years after the person’s release from imprisonment after conviction for the offence or, if the person is not then imprisoned or subject to imprisonment, after the person’s conviction for or discharge from the offence; and (b) any prohibited firearm, restricted firearm, prohibited weapon, prohibited device and prohibited ammunition for life.
-- A thing in both (a) and (b) (prohibited ammunition is ammunition: s 84(1)) is prohibited for life: life satisfies the floor of (a) (fork F-109-ammo).
-- src:2298 | Duration of prohibition order — first offence
-- src:2299 | (2) An order made under subsection (1) shall, in the case of a first conviction for or discharge from the offence to which the order relates, prohibit the person from possessing
-- src:2300 | (a) any firearm, other than a prohibited firearm or restricted firearm, and any crossbow, restricted weapon, firearm part, ammunition and explosive substance during the period that
-- src:2301 | (i) begins on the day on which the order is made, and
-- src:2302 | (ii) ends not earlier than ten years after the person’s release from imprisonment after conviction for the offence or, if the person is not then imprisoned or subject to imprisonment, after the person’s conviction for or discharge from the offence; and
-- src:2303 | (b) any prohibited firearm, restricted firearm, prohibited weapon, prohibited device and prohibited ammunition for life.
@ref s 109(2) (src:2298-2303)
GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
      `it is the first conviction for or discharge from the offence to which the order relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is imprisoned or subject to imprisonment for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the person’s release from imprisonment after conviction for the offence` IS A DATE
      `the day of the person’s conviction for or discharge from the offence` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 109 period of the prohibition`
`s 109(2) the period for which the order prohibits the thing, in the case of a first conviction or discharge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is the first conviction for or discharge from the offence to which the order relates` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of a first conviction for or discharge from the offence to which the order relates" (subsection (3) governs any other case)
        IF `the thing is one that paragraph (b) names` THEN JUST `s 109 period: for life`
        IF `the thing is one that paragraph (a) names` THEN JUST (`s 109 period: ending not earlier than` (`add years` `the day from which ten years run` 10))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the thing is not one that the paragraphs name
    WHERE
        -- (b) any prohibited firearm, restricted firearm, prohibited weapon, prohibited device and prohibited ammunition
        `the thing is one that paragraph (b) names` MEANS
               `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a restricted firearm`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited weapon`
               OR `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a prohibited device` `the kind of thing`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: prohibited ammunition`
        -- (a) any firearm, other than a prohibited firearm or restricted firearm, and any crossbow, restricted weapon, firearm part, ammunition and explosive substance
        `the thing is one that paragraph (a) names` MEANS
               `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a non-restricted firearm`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a cross-bow`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a restricted weapon`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a firearm part`
               OR `s 84(1) the kind of thing is ammunition or prohibited ammunition` `the kind of thing`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: an explosive substance`
        -- ten years after the person’s release from imprisonment after conviction for the offence or, if the person is not then imprisoned or subject to imprisonment, after the person’s conviction for or discharge from the offence
        `the day from which ten years run` MEANS
            IF `the person is imprisoned or subject to imprisonment for the offence`
            THEN `the day of the person’s release from imprisonment after conviction for the offence`
            ELSE `the day of the person’s conviction for or discharge from the offence`

-- (3) In any case other than a case described in subsection (2): any firearm, cross-bow, restricted weapon, firearm part, ammunition and explosive substance for life.
-- Subsection (3) names no prohibited weapon and no prohibited device (subsections (1) and (2)(b) do) (Finding): for those the text gives no period (NOTHING).
-- src:2304 | Duration of prohibition order — subsequent offences
-- src:2305 | (3) An order made under subsection (1) shall, in any case other than a case described in subsection (2), prohibit the person from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, restricted weapon, firearm part, ammunition and explosive substance for life.
@ref s 109(3) (src:2304-2305)
GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
      `it is the first conviction for or discharge from the offence to which the order relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 109 period of the prohibition`
`s 109(3) the period for which the order prohibits the thing, in any other case` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is the first conviction for or discharge from the offence to which the order relates` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any case other than a case described in subsection (2)" (subsection (2) governs a first conviction or discharge)
        IF `the thing is one that the subsection names` THEN JUST `s 109 period: for life`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (3) does not name this thing (a prohibited weapon or a prohibited device), and subsection (1) hands the period to subsections (2) and (3)
    WHERE
        -- any firearm, cross-bow, restricted weapon, firearm part, ammunition and explosive substance
        `the thing is one that the subsection names` MEANS
               `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a firearm` `the kind of thing`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a cross-bow`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a restricted weapon`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a firearm part`
               OR `s 84(1) the kind of thing is ammunition or prohibited ammunition` `the kind of thing`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: an explosive substance`

-- Subsections (2) and (3) together: which of them governs a thing is decided by whether it is the first conviction or discharge.
-- src:2298 | Duration of prohibition order — first offence
-- src:2299 | (2) An order made under subsection (1) shall, in the case of a first conviction for or discharge from the offence to which the order relates, prohibit the person from possessing
-- src:2300 | (a) any firearm, other than a prohibited firearm or restricted firearm, and any crossbow, restricted weapon, firearm part, ammunition and explosive substance during the period that
-- src:2301 | (i) begins on the day on which the order is made, and
-- src:2302 | (ii) ends not earlier than ten years after the person’s release from imprisonment after conviction for the offence or, if the person is not then imprisoned or subject to imprisonment, after the person’s conviction for or discharge from the offence; and
-- src:2303 | (b) any prohibited firearm, restricted firearm, prohibited weapon, prohibited device and prohibited ammunition for life.
-- src:2304 | Duration of prohibition order — subsequent offences
-- src:2305 | (3) An order made under subsection (1) shall, in any case other than a case described in subsection (2), prohibit the person from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, restricted weapon, firearm part, ammunition and explosive substance for life.
@ref s 109(2) and (3) (src:2298-2305)
GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
      `it is the first conviction for or discharge from the offence to which the order relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is imprisoned or subject to imprisonment for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the person’s release from imprisonment after conviction for the offence` IS A DATE
      `the day of the person’s conviction for or discharge from the offence` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 109 period of the prohibition`
`s 109(2) and (3) the period for which the order prohibits the thing` MEANS
    IF `it is the first conviction for or discharge from the offence to which the order relates`
    THEN `s 109(2) the period for which the order prohibits the thing, in the case of a first conviction or discharge` `the kind of thing` `it is the first conviction for or discharge from the offence to which the order relates` `the person is imprisoned or subject to imprisonment for the offence` `the day of the person’s release from imprisonment after conviction for the offence` `the day of the person’s conviction for or discharge from the offence`
    ELSE `s 109(3) the period for which the order prohibits the thing, in any other case` `the kind of thing` `it is the first conviction for or discharge from the offence to which the order relates`

-- (4) In subparagraph (2)(a)(ii), release from imprisonment means release from confinement by reason of expiration of sentence, commencement of statutory release or grant of parole.
-- src:2306 | Definition of release from imprisonment
-- src:2307 | (4) In subparagraph (2)(a)(ii), release from imprisonment means release from confinement by reason of expiration of sentence, commencement of statutory release or grant of parole.
@ref s 109(4) (src:2306-2307)
DECLARE `s 109(4) release from confinement` IS ONE OF
    `s 109(4) release: by reason of expiration of sentence`
    `s 109(4) release: by reason of commencement of statutory release`
    `s 109(4) release: by reason of grant of parole`
    `s 109(4) release: by reason of something else`

@ref s 109(4) (src:2306-2307)
GIVEN `the release` IS A `s 109(4) release from confinement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109(4) release from imprisonment` MEANS
    IF `the release` EQUALS `s 109(4) release: by reason of something else`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "release from imprisonment means release from confinement by reason of expiration of sentence, commencement of statutory release or grant of parole"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (5) Sections 113 to 117 apply in respect of every order made under subsection (1).
-- src:2308 | Application of ss. 113 to 117
-- src:2309 | (5) Sections 113 to 117 apply in respect of every order made under subsection (1).
@ref s 109(5) (src:2308-2309)
GIVEN `the section` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109(5) the section applies in respect of every order made under subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the section`'s `section` AT LEAST 113 AND `the section`'s `section` AT MOST 117
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Sections 113 to 117 apply in respect of every order made under subsection (1)" (it names no other section)

§ `Section 110 -- Discretionary prohibition order`

-- (1) Where a person is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of (a) an offence, other than an offence referred to in any of paragraphs 109(1)(a) to (c.1), in the commission of which violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted, or
-- (b) an offence that involves, or the subject-matter of which is, a firearm ... and, at the time of the offence, the person was not prohibited by any order ... from possessing any such thing, the court shall consider whether it is desirable, in the interests of safety, to make an order, and if it decides that it is so desirable, shall so order.
-- src:2310 | Discretionary prohibition order
-- src:2311 | 110 (1) Where a person is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of
-- src:2312 | (a) an offence, other than an offence referred to in any of paragraphs 109(1)(a) to (c.1), in the commission of which violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted, or
-- src:2313 | (b) an offence that involves, or the subject-matter of which is, a firearm, a cross-bow, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance and, at the time of the offence, the person was not prohibited by any order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament from possessing any such thing,
-- src:2314 | the court that sentences the person or directs that the person be discharged, as the case may be, shall, in addition to any other punishment that may be imposed for that offence or any other condition prescribed in the order of discharge, consider whether it is desirable, in the interests of the safety of the person or of any other person, to make an order prohibiting the person from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all such things, and if the court decides that it is so desirable, the court shall so order.
@ref s 110(1) (src:2310-2314)
GIVEN `how the person comes before the court for sentence` IS A `s 109(1) how the person comes before the court for sentence`
      `violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 3.01(1) the offence counts as an offence in the commission of which violence is used, threatened or attempted against any person or class of persons` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 109(1) the offence is referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (c.1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the kind of thing` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
      `the offence involves, or its subject-matter is, that thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time of the offence the person was prohibited by an order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament from possessing any such thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110(1) the court must consider whether it is desirable to make a prohibition order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `how the person comes before the court for sentence` EQUALS `s 109(1) the person is neither convicted nor discharged under section 730` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of" (a "where" that fails)
        IF `limb (b)` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `limb (a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `limb (a)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the answer of section 3.01 or of paragraphs 109(1)(a) to (c.1) is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of" an offence within paragraph (a) or (b) (an offence outside them: no duty to consider arises under this subsection)
    WHERE
        -- (a) an offence, other than an offence referred to in any of paragraphs 109(1)(a) to (c.1), in the commission of which violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted
        `limb (a)` MEANS `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST (`s 84(1) some limb holds` (LIST (JUST `violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted in the commission of the offence`), `s 3.01(1) the offence counts as an offence in the commission of which violence is used, threatened or attempted against any person or class of persons`)), (`s 84(1) the answer reversed` `s 109(1) the offence is referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (c.1)`))
        -- (b) an offence that involves, or the subject-matter of which is, a firearm, a cross-bow, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance and, at the time of the offence, the person was not prohibited
        `limb (b)` MEANS
                (`the thing is one that the paragraph names`)
            AND `the offence involves, or its subject-matter is, that thing`
            AND (NOT `at the time of the offence the person was prohibited by an order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament from possessing any such thing`)
        `the thing is one that the paragraph names` MEANS
               `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a firearm` `the kind of thing`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a cross-bow`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited weapon`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a restricted weapon`
               OR `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a prohibited device` `the kind of thing`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a firearm part`
               OR `s 84(1) the kind of thing is ammunition or prohibited ammunition` `the kind of thing`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: an explosive substance`

-- ... and if the court decides that it is so desirable, the court shall so order.
-- src:2310 | Discretionary prohibition order
-- src:2311 | 110 (1) Where a person is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of
-- src:2312 | (a) an offence, other than an offence referred to in any of paragraphs 109(1)(a) to (c.1), in the commission of which violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted, or
-- src:2313 | (b) an offence that involves, or the subject-matter of which is, a firearm, a cross-bow, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance and, at the time of the offence, the person was not prohibited by any order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament from possessing any such thing,
-- src:2314 | the court that sentences the person or directs that the person be discharged, as the case may be, shall, in addition to any other punishment that may be imposed for that offence or any other condition prescribed in the order of discharge, consider whether it is desirable, in the interests of the safety of the person or of any other person, to make an order prohibiting the person from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all such things, and if the court decides that it is so desirable, the court shall so order.
@ref s 110(1), the order (src:2310-2314)
GIVEN `s 110(1) the court must consider whether it is desirable to make a prohibition order` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court decides that it is so desirable, in the interests of the safety of the person or of any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110(1) the court must make a prohibition order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 110(1) the court must consider whether it is desirable to make a prohibition order` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the court decides that it is so desirable, in the interests of the safety of the person or of any other person` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 110(1) the court must consider whether it is desirable to make a prohibition order` EQUALS NOTHING AND `the court decides that it is so desirable, in the interests of the safety of the person or of any other person` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the duty to consider arises is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the court decides that it is so desirable, the court shall so order" (the court did not decide that it is desirable, or no duty to consider arose)

-- src:2310 | Discretionary prohibition order
-- src:2311 | 110 (1) Where a person is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of
-- src:2312 | (a) an offence, other than an offence referred to in any of paragraphs 109(1)(a) to (c.1), in the commission of which violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted, or
-- src:2313 | (b) an offence that involves, or the subject-matter of which is, a firearm, a cross-bow, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance and, at the time of the offence, the person was not prohibited by any order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament from possessing any such thing,
-- src:2314 | the court that sentences the person or directs that the person be discharged, as the case may be, shall, in addition to any other punishment that may be imposed for that offence or any other condition prescribed in the order of discharge, consider whether it is desirable, in the interests of the safety of the person or of any other person, to make an order prohibiting the person from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all such things, and if the court decides that it is so desirable, the court shall so order.
@ref s 110(1), the duties (src:2310-2314)
GIVEN `the court decides that it is so desirable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 109 act of the court or of a justice`
`s 110(1) the duty of the court to consider, and to make the order it decides is desirable` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 110 consider whether it is desirable to make an order prohibiting the person from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance`
    HENCE (
        IF `the court decides that it is so desirable`
        THEN PARTY `the court`
             MUST `s 110 make the order that the court decides is desirable`
        ELSE FULFILLED)

§§ `Section 110(2) to (5) -- Duration, reasons, definitions`

-- (2) The order begins on the day on which it is made and ends not later than ten years after the person’s release from imprisonment after conviction for the offence or, if the person is not then imprisoned or subject to imprisonment, after the person’s conviction for or discharge from the offence.
-- (2.1) Despite subsection (2), the order may be imposed for life or for any shorter duration if, in the commission of the offence, violence was used, threatened or attempted against (a) the person’s intimate partner; (b) a child or parent of the person or of anyone referred to in paragraph (a); or (c) any person who resides with the person or with anyone referred to in paragraph (a) or (b).
DECLARE `s 110 longest duration of the order` IS ONE OF
    `s 110 duration: life or any shorter duration`
    `s 110 duration: ending not later than` HAS `the latest day on which the order may end` IS A DATE

-- src:2315 | Duration of prohibition order
-- src:2316 | (2) An order made under subsection (1) against a person begins on the day on which the order is made and ends not later than ten years after the person’s release from imprisonment after conviction for the offence to which the order relates or, if the person is not then imprisoned or subject to imprisonment, after the person’s conviction for or discharge from the offence.
@ref s 110(2) (src:2315-2316)
GIVEN `the person is imprisoned or subject to imprisonment for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the person’s release from imprisonment after conviction for the offence` IS A DATE
      `the day of the person’s conviction for or discharge from the offence` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 110(2) the latest day on which the order may end` MEANS
    `add years`
        (IF `the person is imprisoned or subject to imprisonment for the offence`
         THEN `the day of the person’s release from imprisonment after conviction for the offence`
         ELSE `the day of the person’s conviction for or discharge from the offence`)
        10

-- src:2317 | Exception
-- src:2318 | (2.1) Despite subsection (2), an order made under subsection (1) may be imposed for life or for any shorter duration if, in the commission of the offence, violence was used, threatened or attempted against
-- src:2319 | (a) the person’s intimate partner;
-- src:2320 | (b) a child or parent of the person or of anyone referred to in paragraph (a); or
-- src:2321 | (c) any person who resides with the person or with anyone referred to in paragraph (a) or (b).
@ref s 110(2.1) (src:2317-2321)
GIVEN `violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 3.01(1) the offence counts as an offence in the commission of which violence is used, threatened or attempted against any person or class of persons` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 intimate partner: the person against whom the violence was used, threatened or attempted is the person’s intimate partner` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person against whom the violence was used, threatened or attempted is a child or parent of the person or of the person’s intimate partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person against whom the violence was used, threatened or attempted resides with the person or with the person’s intimate partner, child or parent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110(2.1) the order may be imposed for life or for any shorter duration` MEANS
    IF `the conditions` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be imposed for life or for any shorter duration if, in the commission of the offence, violence was used, threatened or attempted against" (a power with an "if" gate: the ruling of 2026-11-12; fork F-110(2.1); subsection (2) governs the other cases)
    WHERE
        `the conditions` MEANS `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST (`s 84(1) some limb holds` (LIST (JUST `violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted in the commission of the offence`), `s 3.01(1) the offence counts as an offence in the commission of which violence is used, threatened or attempted against any person or class of persons`)), (`s 84(1) some limb holds` (LIST `s 2 intimate partner: the person against whom the violence was used, threatened or attempted is the person’s intimate partner`, (JUST `the person against whom the violence was used, threatened or attempted is a child or parent of the person or of the person’s intimate partner`), (JUST `the person against whom the violence was used, threatened or attempted resides with the person or with the person’s intimate partner, child or parent`))))

-- src:2315 | Duration of prohibition order
-- src:2316 | (2) An order made under subsection (1) against a person begins on the day on which the order is made and ends not later than ten years after the person’s release from imprisonment after conviction for the offence to which the order relates or, if the person is not then imprisoned or subject to imprisonment, after the person’s conviction for or discharge from the offence.
-- src:2317 | Exception
-- src:2318 | (2.1) Despite subsection (2), an order made under subsection (1) may be imposed for life or for any shorter duration if, in the commission of the offence, violence was used, threatened or attempted against
-- src:2319 | (a) the person’s intimate partner;
-- src:2320 | (b) a child or parent of the person or of anyone referred to in paragraph (a); or
-- src:2321 | (c) any person who resides with the person or with anyone referred to in paragraph (a) or (b).
@ref s 110(2) and (2.1) (src:2315-2321)
GIVEN `s 110(2.1) the order may be imposed for life or for any shorter duration` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is imprisoned or subject to imprisonment for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the person’s release from imprisonment after conviction for the offence` IS A DATE
      `the day of the person’s conviction for or discharge from the offence` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `s 110 longest duration of the order`
`s 110(2) and (2.1) the longest duration of the order` MEANS
    IF `s 110(2.1) the order may be imposed for life or for any shorter duration` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN `s 110 duration: life or any shorter duration`
    ELSE `s 110 duration: ending not later than` (`s 110(2) the latest day on which the order may end` `the person is imprisoned or subject to imprisonment for the offence` `the day of the person’s release from imprisonment after conviction for the offence` `the day of the person’s conviction for or discharge from the offence`)

-- (3) Where the court does not make an order under subsection (1), or where the court does make such an order but does not prohibit the possession of everything referred to in that subsection, the court shall include in the record a statement of the court’s reasons for not doing so.
-- src:2322 | Reasons
-- src:2323 | (3) Where the court does not make an order under subsection (1), or where the court does make such an order but does not prohibit the possession of everything referred to in that subsection, the court shall include in the record a statement of the court’s reasons for not doing so.
@ref s 110(3) (src:2322-2323)
GIVEN `the court does not make an order under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court makes an order under subsection (1) but does not prohibit the possession of everything referred to in that subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110(3) the court must include in the record a statement of its reasons` MEANS
    IF     `the court does not make an order under subsection (1)`
        OR `the court makes an order under subsection (1) but does not prohibit the possession of everything referred to in that subsection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the court does not make an order under subsection (1), or where the court does make such an order but does not prohibit the possession of everything" (a "where" that fails)

@ref s 110(3), the duty (src:2322-2323)
GIVEN `the court does not make an order, or does not prohibit everything` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 109 act of the court or of a justice`
`s 110(3) the duty of the court to include its reasons in the record` MEANS
    IF `the court does not make an order, or does not prohibit everything`
    THEN PARTY `the court`
         MUST `s 110 include in the record a statement of the court’s reasons for not making the order or not prohibiting everything`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (4) In subsection (2), release from imprisonment means release from confinement by reason of expiration of sentence, commencement of statutory release or grant of parole.
-- src:2324 | Definition of release from imprisonment
-- src:2325 | (4) In subsection (2), release from imprisonment means release from confinement by reason of expiration of sentence, commencement of statutory release or grant of parole.
@ref s 110(4) (src:2324-2325)
DECLARE `s 110(4) release from confinement` IS ONE OF
    `s 110(4) release: by reason of expiration of sentence`
    `s 110(4) release: by reason of commencement of statutory release`
    `s 110(4) release: by reason of grant of parole`
    `s 110(4) release: by reason of something else`

@ref s 110(4) (src:2324-2325)
GIVEN `the release` IS A `s 110(4) release from confinement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110(4) release from imprisonment` MEANS
    IF `the release` EQUALS `s 110(4) release: by reason of something else`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "release from imprisonment means release from confinement by reason of expiration of sentence, commencement of statutory release or grant of parole"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (5) Sections 113 to 117 apply in respect of every order made under subsection (1).
-- src:2326 | Application of ss. 113 to 117
-- src:2327 | (5) Sections 113 to 117 apply in respect of every order made under subsection (1).
@ref s 110(5) (src:2326-2327)
GIVEN `the section` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110(5) the section applies in respect of every order made under subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the section`'s `section` AT LEAST 113 AND `the section`'s `section` AT MOST 117
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Sections 113 to 117 apply in respect of every order made under subsection (1)" (it names no other section)

§ `Section 110.1 -- Application for emergency prohibition order`

-- (1) Any person may make an ex parte application to a provincial court judge for an order prohibiting another person from possessing any firearm, ... or explosive substance, or all such things, if the person believes on reasonable grounds that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person against whom the order is sought or of any other person that the person against whom the order is sought should possess any such thing.
-- src:2328 | Application for emergency prohibition order
-- src:2329 | 110.1 (1) Any person may make an ex parte application to a provincial court judge for an order prohibiting another person from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all such things, if the person believes on reasonable grounds that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person against whom the order is sought or of any other person that the person against whom the order is sought should possess any such thing.
@ref s 110.1(1) (src:2328-2329)
GIVEN `the applicant believes on reasonable grounds that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person against whom the order is sought or of any other person that that person should possess any such thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110.1(1) any person may make an ex parte application to a provincial court judge for an order` MEANS
    IF `the applicant believes on reasonable grounds that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person against whom the order is sought or of any other person that that person should possess any such thing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the person believes on reasonable grounds that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety" (a power with an "if" gate: the ruling of 2026-11-12; fork F-110.1(1))

-- (2) The provincial court judge may hold the hearing of an application made under subsection (1) in private if the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the applicant or of anyone known to the applicant.
-- src:2330 | Hearing in private
-- src:2331 | (2) The provincial court judge may hold the hearing of an application made under subsection (1) in private if the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the applicant or of anyone known to the applicant.
@ref s 110.1(2) (src:2330-2331)
GIVEN `the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the applicant or of anyone known to the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110.1(2) the provincial court judge may hold the hearing in private` MEANS
    IF `the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the applicant or of anyone known to the applicant`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the applicant" (a power with an "if" gate: the ruling of 2026-11-12; fork F-110.1(2))

-- (3) If, at the conclusion of a hearing of an application made under subsection (1), the provincial court judge is satisfied that the circumstances referred to in that subsection exist and that an order should be made without delay to ensure the immediate protection of any person, the judge shall make an order ... for a period not exceeding 30 days, as is specified in the order, beginning on the day on which the order is made.
-- src:2332 | Emergency prohibition order
-- src:2333 | (3) If, at the conclusion of a hearing of an application made under subsection (1), the provincial court judge is satisfied that the circumstances referred to in that subsection exist and that an order should be made without delay to ensure the immediate protection of any person, the judge shall make an order prohibiting the person against whom the order is sought from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all such things, for a period not exceeding 30 days, as is specified in the order, beginning on the day on which the order is made.
@ref s 110.1(3) (src:2332-2333)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied that the circumstances referred to in subsection (1) exist` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that an order should be made without delay to ensure the immediate protection of any person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110.1(3) the provincial court judge must make an emergency prohibition order` MEANS
    IF     `the judge is satisfied that the circumstances referred to in subsection (1) exist`
       AND `the judge is satisfied that an order should be made without delay to ensure the immediate protection of any person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, at the conclusion of a hearing of an application made under subsection (1), the provincial court judge is satisfied" (an "if" that fails; a duty, not a power: fork F-110.1(3))

-- the period of the order: "for a period not exceeding 30 days, as is specified in the order, beginning on the day on which the order is made"
-- src:2332 | Emergency prohibition order
-- src:2333 | (3) If, at the conclusion of a hearing of an application made under subsection (1), the provincial court judge is satisfied that the circumstances referred to in that subsection exist and that an order should be made without delay to ensure the immediate protection of any person, the judge shall make an order prohibiting the person against whom the order is sought from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all such things, for a period not exceeding 30 days, as is specified in the order, beginning on the day on which the order is made.
@ref s 110.1(3), the period (src:2332-2333)
GIVEN `the period specified in the order` IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110.1(3) the period specified in the order is within the limit of thirty days` MEANS
    IF     `the period specified in the order`'s years EQUALS 0
       AND `the period specified in the order`'s months EQUALS 0
       AND `the period specified in the order`'s days AT MOST 30
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period not exceeding 30 days" (a period the text states: ruling (a) of 2026-11-05; the other reading is NOTHING, a stated period being among the limits of a grant on the rule of 2026-10-29; fork F-30-days)

-- src:2332 | Emergency prohibition order
-- src:2333 | (3) If, at the conclusion of a hearing of an application made under subsection (1), the provincial court judge is satisfied that the circumstances referred to in that subsection exist and that an order should be made without delay to ensure the immediate protection of any person, the judge shall make an order prohibiting the person against whom the order is sought from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all such things, for a period not exceeding 30 days, as is specified in the order, beginning on the day on which the order is made.
@ref s 110.1(3), the duty (src:2332-2333)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied, as subsection (3) says` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 109 act of the court or of a justice`
`s 110.1(3) the duty of the provincial court judge to make an emergency prohibition order` MEANS
    IF `the judge is satisfied, as subsection (3) says`
    THEN PARTY `a provincial court judge`
         MUST `s 110.1 make an emergency prohibition order`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (4) A copy of the order shall be served on the person to whom the order is addressed in the manner that the provincial court judge directs or in accordance with the rules of court.
-- src:2334 | Service of order
-- src:2335 | (4) A copy of the order shall be served on the person to whom the order is addressed in the manner that the provincial court judge directs or in accordance with the rules of court.
@ref s 110.1(4) (src:2334-2335)
GIVEN `an order has been made under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110.1(4) a copy of the order must be served on the person to whom it is addressed` MEANS
    IF `an order has been made under subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says nothing of service where no order has been made (and it names no one who serves)

-- (5) If a provincial court judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that a person who is subject to an order made under subsection (3) possesses, in a building, receptacle or place, any thing the possession of which is prohibited by the order and that it is not desirable ... the judge may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to search the building, receptacle or place and seize any such thing, and every authorization, licence or registration certificate relating to any such thing ...
-- src:2336 | Warrant to search and seize
-- src:2337 | (5) If a provincial court judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that a person who is subject to an order made under subsection (3) possesses, in a building, receptacle or place, any thing the possession of which is prohibited by the order and that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person, or of any other person, for the person to possess the thing, the judge may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to search the building, receptacle or place and seize any such thing, and every authorization, licence or registration certificate relating to any such thing, that is held by or in the possession of the person.
@ref s 110.1(5) (src:2336-2337)
GIVEN `the person is subject to an order made under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person possesses, in a building, receptacle or place, a thing the possession of which is prohibited by the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person, or of any other person, for the person to possess the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110.1(5) the provincial court judge may issue a warrant to search and seize` MEANS
    IF     `the person is subject to an order made under subsection (3)`
       AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person possesses, in a building, receptacle or place, a thing the possession of which is prohibited by the order`
       AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person, or of any other person, for the person to possess the thing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a provincial court judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe" (a power with an "if" gate: the ruling of 2026-11-12; fork F-110.1(5))

-- (6) If, in respect of a person who is subject to an order made under subsection (3), a peace officer is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that it is not desirable ... for the person to possess any thing the possession of which is prohibited by the order, the peace officer may — if the grounds for obtaining a warrant under subsection (5) exist but, by reason of a possible danger to the safety of the person or any other person, it would not be practicable to obtain a warrant — search for and seize any such thing ...
-- src:2338 | Search and seizure without warrant
-- src:2339 | (6) If, in respect of a person who is subject to an order made under subsection (3), a peace officer is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that it is not desirable, in the interests of the safety of the person, or of any other person, for the person to possess any thing the possession of which is prohibited by the order, the peace officer may — if the grounds for obtaining a warrant under subsection (5) exist but, by reason of a possible danger to the safety of the person or any other person, it would not be practicable to obtain a warrant — search for and seize any such thing, and any authorization, licence or registration certificate relating to any such thing, that is held by or in the possession of the person.
@ref s 110.1(6) (src:2338-2339)
GIVEN `the person is subject to an order made under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person, or of any other person, for the person to possess a thing the possession of which is prohibited by the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the grounds for obtaining a warrant under subsection (5) exist` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by reason of a possible danger to the safety of the person or any other person, it would not be practicable to obtain a warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110.1(6) the peace officer may search for and seize without a warrant` MEANS
    IF     `the person is subject to an order made under subsection (3)`
       AND `the peace officer is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person, or of any other person, for the person to possess a thing the possession of which is prohibited by the order`
       AND `the grounds for obtaining a warrant under subsection (5) exist`
       AND `by reason of a possible danger to the safety of the person or any other person, it would not be practicable to obtain a warrant`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the grounds for obtaining a warrant under subsection (5) exist but, by reason of a possible danger to the safety of the person or any other person, it would not be practicable to obtain a warrant" (a power with an "if" gate: the ruling of 2026-11-12)

-- (7) A peace officer who executes a warrant referred to in subsection (5) or who conducts a search without a warrant under subsection (6) shall immediately make a report to a justice having jurisdiction ... showing (a) in the case of an execution of a warrant, the things or documents, if any, seized and the date of execution of the warrant; and (b) in the case of a search conducted without a warrant, the grounds on which it was concluded that the peace officer was entitled to conduct the search, and the things or documents, if any, seized.
-- src:2340 | Report to justice
-- src:2341 | (7) A peace officer who executes a warrant referred to in subsection (5) or who conducts a search without a warrant under subsection (6) shall immediately make a report to a justice having jurisdiction in respect of the matter and, in the case of an execution of a warrant, jurisdiction in the province in which the warrant was issued, showing
@ref s 110.1(7) (src:2340-2341)
GIVEN `the peace officer executes a warrant referred to in subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer conducts a search without a warrant under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110.1(7) the peace officer must make a report to a justice` MEANS
    IF     `the peace officer executes a warrant referred to in subsection (5)`
        OR `the peace officer conducts a search without a warrant under subsection (6)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A peace officer who executes a warrant referred to in subsection (5) or who conducts a search without a warrant under subsection (6) shall" (the duty is of that peace officer only)

DECLARE `s 110.1(7) item of the report` IS ONE OF
    `s 110.1(7) the things or documents, if any, seized`
    `s 110.1(7) the date of execution of the warrant`
    `s 110.1(7) the grounds on which it was concluded that the peace officer was entitled to conduct the search`

-- src:2340 | Report to justice
-- src:2341 | (7) A peace officer who executes a warrant referred to in subsection (5) or who conducts a search without a warrant under subsection (6) shall immediately make a report to a justice having jurisdiction in respect of the matter and, in the case of an execution of a warrant, jurisdiction in the province in which the warrant was issued, showing
-- src:2342 | (a) in the case of an execution of a warrant, the things or documents, if any, seized and the date of execution of the warrant; and
-- src:2343 | (b) in the case of a search conducted without a warrant, the grounds on which it was concluded that the peace officer was entitled to conduct the search, and the things or documents, if any, seized.
@ref s 110.1(7)(a) and (b) (src:2340-2343)
GIVEN `the report is of an execution of a warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report is of a search conducted without a warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 110.1(7) item of the report`
`s 110.1(7) what the report must show` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the report is of an execution of a warrant` THEN LIST `s 110.1(7) the things or documents, if any, seized`, `s 110.1(7) the date of execution of the warrant`
        IF `the report is of a search conducted without a warrant` THEN LIST `s 110.1(7) the grounds on which it was concluded that the peace officer was entitled to conduct the search`, `s 110.1(7) the things or documents, if any, seized`
        OTHERWISE EMPTY

-- The text says "immediately", and no number: the rule has no WITHIN (reading A; reading B would be WITHIN 0: fork F-immediately).
-- src:2340 | Report to justice
-- src:2341 | (7) A peace officer who executes a warrant referred to in subsection (5) or who conducts a search without a warrant under subsection (6) shall immediately make a report to a justice having jurisdiction in respect of the matter and, in the case of an execution of a warrant, jurisdiction in the province in which the warrant was issued, showing
@ref s 110.1(7), the duty (src:2340-2341)
GIVEN `subsection (7) applies to the peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 109 act of the court or of a justice`
`s 110.1(7) the duty of the peace officer to make a report to a justice` MEANS
    IF `subsection (7) applies to the peace officer`
    THEN PARTY `a peace officer`
         MUST `s 110.1 make a report to a justice`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (8) Any things or documents seized under subsection (5) or (6) from a person against whom an order has been made under subsection (3) shall be returned to the person and any things or documents surrendered by the person in accordance with the order shall be returned to the person
-- (a) if no date is fixed under subsection 110.4(1) for the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1) in respect of the person, as soon as feasible after the end of the period specified in the order made against the person under subsection (3);
-- (b) if a date is fixed for the hearing but no order is made against the person under subsection 111(5), as soon as feasible after the final disposition of the application; or
-- (c) despite paragraphs (a) and (b), if the order made against the person under subsection (3) is revoked, as soon as feasible after the day on which it is revoked.
DECLARE `s 110.1(8) the occasion for returning the things and documents` IS ONE OF
    `s 110.1(8) as soon as feasible after the end of the period specified in the order`
    `s 110.1(8) as soon as feasible after the final disposition of the application`
    `s 110.1(8) as soon as feasible after the day on which the order is revoked`

-- src:2344 | Return of things and documents
-- src:2345 | (8) Any things or documents seized under subsection (5) or (6) from a person against whom an order has been made under subsection (3) shall be returned to the person and any things or documents surrendered by the person in accordance with the order shall be returned to the person
-- src:2346 | (a) if no date is fixed under subsection 110.4(1) for the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1) in respect of the person, as soon as feasible after the end of the period specified in the order made against the person under subsection (3);
-- src:2347 | (b) if a date is fixed for the hearing but no order is made against the person under subsection 111(5), as soon as feasible after the final disposition of the application; or
-- src:2348 | (c) despite paragraphs (a) and (b), if the order made against the person under subsection (3) is revoked, as soon as feasible after the day on which it is revoked.
@ref s 110.1(8) (src:2344-2348)
GIVEN `a date is fixed under subsection 110.4(1) for the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1) in respect of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order is made against the person under subsection 111(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order made against the person under subsection (3) is revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 110.1(8) the occasion for returning the things and documents`
`s 110.1(8) the occasion on which the things and documents must be returned to the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the order made against the person under subsection (3) is revoked` THEN JUST `s 110.1(8) as soon as feasible after the day on which the order is revoked`   -- (c) "despite paragraphs (a) and (b)"
        IF NOT (`a date is fixed under subsection 110.4(1) for the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1) in respect of the person`) THEN JUST `s 110.1(8) as soon as feasible after the end of the period specified in the order`   -- (a)
        IF NOT (`an order is made against the person under subsection 111(5)`) THEN JUST `s 110.1(8) as soon as feasible after the final disposition of the application`   -- (b): a date is fixed but no order is made under subsection 111(5)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a date is fixed and an order is made under subsection 111(5): the text gives no occasion for returning the things in that case

-- (9) Sections 113, 114 and 116 apply in respect of every order made under subsection (3).
-- src:2349 | Application of sections 113, 114 and 116
-- src:2350 | (9) Sections 113, 114 and 116 apply in respect of every order made under subsection (3).
@ref s 110.1(9) (src:2349-2350)
GIVEN `the section` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110.1(9) the section applies in respect of every order made under subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF `the section`'s `section` EQUALS 113 OR `the section`'s `section` EQUALS 114 OR `the section`'s `section` EQUALS 116
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Sections 113, 114 and 116 apply in respect of every order made under subsection (3)" (it names no other section)

-- (10) In this section and sections 110.4, 111, 112, 117.0101, 117.0104, 117.011 and 117.012, provincial court judge means a provincial court judge having jurisdiction in the territorial division where the person against whom the application for an order was brought resides.
-- src:2351 | Definition of provincial court judge
-- src:2352 | (10) In this section and sections 110.4, 111, 112, 117.0101, 117.0104, 117.011 and 117.012, provincial court judge means a provincial court judge having jurisdiction in the territorial division where the person against whom the application for an order was brought resides.
@ref s 110.1(10) (src:2351-2352)
GIVEN `the section` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the provincial court judge has jurisdiction in the territorial division where the person against whom the application for an order was brought resides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110.1(10) provincial court judge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the section is one that the subsection names`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In this section and sections 110.4, 111, 112, 117.0101, 117.0104, 117.011 and 117.012"
        IF `the provincial court judge has jurisdiction in the territorial division where the person against whom the application for an order was brought resides` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provincial court judge means a provincial court judge having jurisdiction in the territorial division where the person against whom the application for an order was brought resides"
    WHERE
        `the section is one that the subsection names` MEANS
               `the section`'s `section` EQUALS 110.1
            OR `the section`'s `section` EQUALS 110.4
            OR `the section`'s `section` EQUALS 111
            OR `the section`'s `section` EQUALS 112
            OR `the section`'s `section` EQUALS 117.0101
            OR `the section`'s `section` EQUALS 117.0104
            OR `the section`'s `section` EQUALS 117.011
            OR `the section`'s `section` EQUALS 117.012

§ `Section 110.2 -- Order denying access to information`

-- (1) If an order is made under subsection 110.1(3), a provincial court judge may, on application by the person who applied for the order or on the judge’s own motion, if the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the person or of anyone known to the person, make an order prohibiting access to, and the disclosure of, any or all of the following: (a) ... (d) ...
-- src:2353 | Order denying access to information
-- src:2354 | 110.2 (1) If an order is made under subsection 110.1(3), a provincial court judge may, on application by the person who applied for the order or on the judge’s own motion, if the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the person or of anyone known to the person, make an order prohibiting access to, and the disclosure of, any or all of the following:
@ref s 110.2(1) (src:2353-2354)
GIVEN `an order is made under subsection 110.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge acts on application by the person who applied for the order or on the judge’s own motion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the person or of anyone known to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110.2(1) a provincial court judge may make an order prohibiting access to, and the disclosure of, information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`an order is made under subsection 110.1(3)`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an order is made under subsection 110.1(3), a provincial court judge may" (a power with an "if" gate: the ruling of 2026-11-12; fork F-110.2(1))
        IF NOT (`the judge acts on application by the person who applied for the order or on the judge’s own motion`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application by the person who applied for the order or on the judge’s own motion" (an "on application" gate, the kind of "when" and "upon", which count as "where": rulings (b) and (c) of 2026-11-05; the other reading is NOTHING, a power limited by its own wording; fork F-110.2(1))
        IF NOT (`the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the person or of anyone known to the person`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the person or of anyone known to the person" (a power with an "if" gate: the ruling of 2026-11-12; fork F-110.2(1))
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 110.2(1) information` IS ONE OF
    `s 110.2(1) information: relating to the order made under subsection 110.1(3)`
    `s 110.2(1) information: relating to a warrant issued under subsection 110.1(5)`
    `s 110.2(1) information: relating to a search and seizure conducted without a warrant under subsection 110.1(6)`
    `s 110.2(1) information: relating to the order made under subsection 110.2(1)`
    `s 110.2(1) information: of another kind`

-- src:2354 | 110.2 (1) If an order is made under subsection 110.1(3), a provincial court judge may, on application by the person who applied for the order or on the judge’s own motion, if the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the person or of anyone known to the person, make an order prohibiting access to, and the disclosure of, any or all of the following:
-- src:2355 | (a) any information relating to the order made under that subsection;
-- src:2356 | (b) any information relating to a warrant issued under subsection 110.1(5);
-- src:2357 | (c) any information relating to a search and seizure conducted without a warrant under subsection 110.1(6); and
-- src:2358 | (d) any information relating to the order made under this subsection.
@ref s 110.2(1)(a) to (d) (src:2354-2358)
GIVEN `the information` IS A `s 110.2(1) information`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110.2(1) the information is within the order that may be made` MEANS
    IF `the information` EQUALS `s 110.2(1) information: of another kind`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "any or all of the following" (the list does not say "only")
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (2) Unless an order made under subsection (1) is revoked earlier, it expires on the day on which the order made under subsection 110.1(3) expires or is revoked.
-- src:2359 | Expiry of order
-- src:2360 | (2) Unless an order made under subsection (1) is revoked earlier, it expires on the day on which the order made under subsection 110.1(3) expires or is revoked.
@ref s 110.2(2) (src:2359-2360)
GIVEN `the order made under subsection (1) is revoked earlier` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the order made under subsection 110.1(3) expires or is revoked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 110.2(2) the day on which the order made under subsection (1) expires` MEANS
    IF `the order made under subsection (1) is revoked earlier`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Unless an order made under subsection (1) is revoked earlier" (it then ends when it is revoked, a day the text does not give)
    ELSE JUST `the day on which the order made under subsection 110.1(3) expires or is revoked`

-- (3) Despite subsection (2), if, before the order made under subsection 110.1(3) expires or is revoked, a date is fixed under subsection 110.4(1) for the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1), an order made under subsection (1) ceases to have effect on (a) the date fixed under subsection 110.4(1); or (b) if the order made under subsection 110.1(3) is revoked before that date, the day on which it is revoked.
-- src:2361 | Exception
-- src:2362 | (3) Despite subsection (2), if, before the order made under subsection 110.1(3) expires or is revoked, a date is fixed under subsection 110.4(1) for the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1), an order made under subsection (1) ceases to have effect on
-- src:2363 | (a) the date fixed under subsection 110.4(1); or
-- src:2364 | (b) if the order made under subsection 110.1(3) is revoked before that date, the day on which it is revoked.
@ref s 110.2(3) (src:2361-2364)
GIVEN `before the order made under subsection 110.1(3) expires or is revoked, a date is fixed under subsection 110.4(1) for the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date fixed under subsection 110.4(1)` IS A DATE
      `the order made under subsection 110.1(3) is revoked before that date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the order made under subsection 110.1(3) is revoked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 110.2(3) the day on which an order made under subsection (1) ceases to have effect` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`before the order made under subsection 110.1(3) expires or is revoked, a date is fixed under subsection 110.4(1) for the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1)`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if, before the order made under subsection 110.1(3) expires or is revoked, a date is fixed under subsection 110.4(1)" (subsection (2) governs the other cases)
        IF `the order made under subsection 110.1(3) is revoked before that date` THEN JUST `the day on which the order made under subsection 110.1(3) is revoked`   -- (b)
        OTHERWISE JUST `the date fixed under subsection 110.4(1)`   -- (a)

-- Subsections (2) and (3) together: when an order made under subsection (1) ends.
-- src:2359 | Expiry of order
-- src:2360 | (2) Unless an order made under subsection (1) is revoked earlier, it expires on the day on which the order made under subsection 110.1(3) expires or is revoked.
-- src:2361 | Exception
-- src:2362 | (3) Despite subsection (2), if, before the order made under subsection 110.1(3) expires or is revoked, a date is fixed under subsection 110.4(1) for the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1), an order made under subsection (1) ceases to have effect on
-- src:2363 | (a) the date fixed under subsection 110.4(1); or
-- src:2364 | (b) if the order made under subsection 110.1(3) is revoked before that date, the day on which it is revoked.
@ref s 110.2(2) and (3) (src:2359-2364)
GIVEN `before the order made under subsection 110.1(3) expires or is revoked, a date is fixed under subsection 110.4(1) for the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date fixed under subsection 110.4(1)` IS A DATE
      `the order made under subsection 110.1(3) is revoked before that date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the order made under subsection 110.1(3) is revoked` IS A DATE
      `the order made under subsection (1) is revoked earlier` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the order made under subsection 110.1(3) expires or is revoked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 110.2(2) and (3) the day on which an order made under subsection (1) ends` MEANS
    IF `before the order made under subsection 110.1(3) expires or is revoked, a date is fixed under subsection 110.4(1) for the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1)`
    THEN `s 110.2(3) the day on which an order made under subsection (1) ceases to have effect` `before the order made under subsection 110.1(3) expires or is revoked, a date is fixed under subsection 110.4(1) for the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1)` `the date fixed under subsection 110.4(1)` `the order made under subsection 110.1(3) is revoked before that date` `the day on which the order made under subsection 110.1(3) is revoked`
    ELSE `s 110.2(2) the day on which the order made under subsection (1) expires` `the order made under subsection (1) is revoked earlier` `the day on which the order made under subsection 110.1(3) expires or is revoked`

-- (4) If an order is made under subsection (1), all documents relating to ... the order ... shall — subject to any terms and conditions that the provincial court judge considers desirable ... — be immediately placed in a packet and sealed by the judge, and the packet shall be kept in the custody of the court in a place to which the public has no access or in any other place that the judge may authorize and shall not be dealt with except in accordance with the terms and conditions specified in the order or as varied under subsection (5).
-- src:2365 | Procedure
-- src:2366 | (4) If an order is made under subsection (1), all documents relating to, as the case may be, the order made under that subsection, the order made under subsection 110.1(3), the warrant issued under subsection 110.1(5) or, in the case of a search and seizure conducted without a warrant under subsection 110.1(6), the report made under subsection 110.1(7) shall — subject to any terms and conditions that the provincial court judge considers desirable in the circumstances, including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing, any term or condition concerning partial disclosure of a document, deletion of any information or the occurrence of a condition — be immediately placed in a packet and sealed by the judge, and the packet shall be kept in the custody of the court in a place to which the public has no access or in any other place that the judge may authorize and shall not be dealt with except in accordance with the terms and conditions specified in the order or as varied under subsection (5).
@ref s 110.2(4) (src:2365-2366)
GIVEN `an order is made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110.2(4) the documents must be placed in a packet and sealed by the judge` MEANS
    IF `an order is made under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an order is made under subsection (1), all documents relating to" (an "if" that fails)

@ref s 110.2(4), the duty (src:2365-2366)
GIVEN `an order is made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 109 act of the court or of a justice`
`s 110.2(4) the duty of the provincial court judge to place the documents in a packet and seal it` MEANS
    IF `an order is made under subsection (1)`
    THEN PARTY `a provincial court judge`
         MUST `s 110.2 place the documents in a packet and seal it`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (5) An application to revoke an order made under subsection (1) or vary any of its terms and conditions may be made to the provincial court judge who made the order or to another provincial court judge.
-- src:2367 | Revocation or variance of order
-- src:2368 | (5) An application to revoke an order made under subsection (1) or vary any of its terms and conditions may be made to the provincial court judge who made the order or to another provincial court judge.
@ref s 110.2(5) (src:2367-2368)
GIVEN `an order was made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made to the provincial court judge who made the order or to another provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110.2(5) an application to revoke the order or vary its terms and conditions may be made to the provincial court judge` MEANS
    IF     `an order was made under subsection (1)`
       AND `the application is made to the provincial court judge who made the order or to another provincial court judge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be made to the provincial court judge who made the order or to another provincial court judge" (it says nothing of an application made elsewhere)

§ `Section 110.3 -- Order to delete identifying information`

-- (1) If an order is made under subsection 110.1(3) or 110.2(1), a provincial court judge may, on application by the person who applied for the order referred to in subsection 110.1(3) or on the judge’s own motion, if the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the person or of anyone known to the person, make an order, subject to any terms and conditions that the judge considers desirable in the circumstances, directing that (a) copies be made ...; (b) any information that could identify the person who applied for the order ... be deleted from those copies; and (c) the documents ... to which the public has access or that are made available to or required to be served on any person are to be the edited copies ...
-- src:2369 | Order to delete identifying information
-- src:2370 | 110.3 (1) If an order is made under subsection 110.1(3) or 110.2(1), a provincial court judge may, on application by the person who applied for the order referred to in subsection 110.1(3) or on the judge’s own motion, if the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the person or of anyone known to the person, make an order, subject to any terms and conditions that the judge considers desirable in the circumstances, directing that
@ref s 110.3(1) (src:2369-2370)
GIVEN `an order is made under subsection 110.1(3) or 110.2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge acts on application by the person who applied for the order referred to in subsection 110.1(3) or on the judge’s own motion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the person or of anyone known to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110.3(1) a provincial court judge may make an order to delete identifying information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`an order is made under subsection 110.1(3) or 110.2(1)`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an order is made under subsection 110.1(3) or 110.2(1), a provincial court judge may" (a power with an "if" gate: the ruling of 2026-11-12; fork F-110.3(1))
        IF NOT (`the judge acts on application by the person who applied for the order referred to in subsection 110.1(3) or on the judge’s own motion`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application by the person who applied for the order referred to in subsection 110.1(3) or on the judge’s own motion" (an "on application" gate, the kind of "when" and "upon", which count as "where": rulings (b) and (c) of 2026-11-05; the other reading is NOTHING, a power limited by its own wording; fork F-110.3(1))
        IF NOT (`the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the person or of anyone known to the person`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the person or of anyone known to the person" (a power with an "if" gate: the ruling of 2026-11-12; fork F-110.3(1))
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 110.3(1) direction` IS ONE OF
    `s 110.3(1) that copies be made of any documents relating to the order made under subsection 110.1(3) or 110.2(1), including the order itself`
    `s 110.3(1) that any information that could identify the person who applied for the order, or anyone known to the person, be deleted from those copies`
    `s 110.3(1) that the documents to which the public has access or that are made available to or required to be served on any person are to be the edited copies`

-- src:2370 | 110.3 (1) If an order is made under subsection 110.1(3) or 110.2(1), a provincial court judge may, on application by the person who applied for the order referred to in subsection 110.1(3) or on the judge’s own motion, if the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the person or of anyone known to the person, make an order, subject to any terms and conditions that the judge considers desirable in the circumstances, directing that
-- src:2371 | (a) copies be made of any documents relating to the order made under subsection 110.1(3) or 110.2(1), as the case may be, including the order itself;
-- src:2372 | (b) any information that could identify the person who applied for the order referred to in subsection 110.1(3) or anyone known to the person be deleted from those copies; and
-- src:2373 | (c) the documents relating to the order made under subsection 110.1(3) or 110.2(1), as the case may be, including the order itself, to which the public has access or that are made available to or required to be served on any person are to be the edited copies referred to in paragraph (b).
@ref s 110.3(1)(a) to (c) (src:2370-2373)
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 110.3(1) direction`
`s 110.3(1) what the order directs` MEANS
    LIST
        `s 110.3(1) that copies be made of any documents relating to the order made under subsection 110.1(3) or 110.2(1), including the order itself`,
        `s 110.3(1) that any information that could identify the person who applied for the order, or anyone known to the person, be deleted from those copies`,
        `s 110.3(1) that the documents to which the public has access or that are made available to or required to be served on any person are to be the edited copies`

-- (2) An order made under subsection (1) may be for any period — definite or indefinite — that the provincial court judge considers necessary to protect the security of the person who applied for the order referred to in subsection 110.1(3) or of anyone known to the person.
-- src:2374 | Duration of order
-- src:2375 | (2) An order made under subsection (1) may be for any period — definite or indefinite — that the provincial court judge considers necessary to protect the security of the person who applied for the order referred to in subsection 110.1(3) or of anyone known to the person.
@ref s 110.3(2) (src:2374-2375)
GIVEN `the judge considers the period necessary to protect the security of the person who applied for the order referred to in subsection 110.1(3) or of anyone known to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110.3(2) the order may be for the period, whether definite or indefinite` MEANS
    IF `the judge considers the period necessary to protect the security of the person who applied for the order referred to in subsection 110.1(3) or of anyone known to the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any period — definite or indefinite — that the provincial court judge considers necessary" (a power limited by a "that" clause, not by an "if" gate, so the guide’s sentence on a grant limited in its own wording applies, not the ruling of 2026-11-12)

-- (3) If an order is made under subsection (1), the originals of all documents that are the subject of the order shall — subject to any terms and conditions that the provincial court judge considers desirable in the circumstances — be immediately placed in a packet and sealed by the judge, and the packet shall be kept in the custody of the court in a place to which the public has no access or in any other place that the judge may authorize and shall not be dealt with except in accordance with the terms and conditions specified in the order or as varied under subsection (4).
-- src:2376 | Procedure
-- src:2377 | (3) If an order is made under subsection (1), the originals of all documents that are the subject of the order shall — subject to any terms and conditions that the provincial court judge considers desirable in the circumstances — be immediately placed in a packet and sealed by the judge, and the packet shall be kept in the custody of the court in a place to which the public has no access or in any other place that the judge may authorize and shall not be dealt with except in accordance with the terms and conditions specified in the order or as varied under subsection (4).
@ref s 110.3(3) (src:2376-2377)
GIVEN `an order is made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110.3(3) the originals must be placed in a packet and sealed by the judge` MEANS
    IF `an order is made under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an order is made under subsection (1), the originals of all documents" (an "if" that fails)

@ref s 110.3(3), the duty (src:2376-2377)
GIVEN `an order is made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 109 act of the court or of a justice`
`s 110.3(3) the duty of the provincial court judge to place the originals in a packet and seal it` MEANS
    IF `an order is made under subsection (1)`
    THEN PARTY `a provincial court judge`
         MUST `s 110.3 place the originals in a packet and seal it`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (4) An application to revoke an order made under subsection (1) or vary any of its terms and conditions may be made to the provincial court judge who made the order or to another provincial court judge.
-- src:2378 | Revocation or variance of order
