-- (5) For greater certainty, if a date is fixed under subsection 110.4(1) for the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1), any order made under this section that is still in force applies in respect of that hearing.
-- src:2380 | Clarification
-- src:2381 | (5) For greater certainty, if a date is fixed under subsection 110.4(1) for the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1), any order made under this section that is still in force applies in respect of that hearing.
@ref s 110.3(5) (src:2380-2381)
GIVEN `a date is fixed under subsection 110.4(1) for the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order made under this section is still in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110.3(5) the order made under this section applies in respect of that hearing` MEANS
    IF     `a date is fixed under subsection 110.4(1) for the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1)`
       AND `the order made under this section is still in force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if a date is fixed under subsection 110.4(1) for the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1), any order made under this section that is still in force applies in respect of that hearing" (it says nothing of other cases)
